R103: the PSpice switch (VSWITCH(Von Voff Ron Roff)) on ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n.
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/pspice_switch/run.sh` (light lane). plain.cir is the
XSPICE pswitch log=TRUE (ngspice-45 source hfvpfb0bgw9819wkb7kzpdaasbd0hd5r,
src/xspice/icm/xtradev/pswitch/cfunc.mod:199-249: R = exp(logmean + c1·u − c3·u³), u = S − 1/2,
c1 = 1.5·ln(Ron/Roff), c3 = 2·ln(Ron/Roff)); mode/vswitch.cir the PSpice VSWITCH that
ngbehavior=ltpsa rewrites into it (src/frontend/inpcompat.c:1264-1417, defaults Ron=1 Roff=1e6
Von=1 Voff=0). Oracle: the closed form of INV-semantics 6.19 (Xyce's VSWITCH, D117):
Rs = exp(Lm + 0.75·Lr·(2S−1) − 0.25·Lr·(2S−1)³), S = (Vc−Voff)/(Von−Voff), clamped to [0, 1].
Result: the two ngspice forms give the same bits at every point, and both equal Xyce's closed form
to rounding (5e-16, 2e-15 at most): the PSpice switch, ngspice's pswitch log=TRUE and Xyce's
VSWITCH are one law, ModelFamily::SwitchLogCubic (CurrentSwitchLogCubic for ISWITCH).
ngspice's own clamps beyond the law: r_on below 1e-3 is raised to 1e-3, r_off above 1e12 lowered
(cfunc.mod:176-177), Von = Voff is nudged apart by 1 mV (185-187), and the control port draws
1e-12 S (r_cntl_in 1e12): a deck outside those bounds is not the family's law on ngspice.

